[block'ORD-0006-explorer'
  [ctx'the spec of EMS-003','.guidelines/.orders/EMS-003/EMS-003.pgml']
  [ctx'the signed model','.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-2D-VIEW.md, section 6']
  [ctx'the trail to the final Explorer','.guidelines/.plan/README.md, section 5, steps 2, 3 and 11']
  [tgt'the 2D view in the Glyph Explorer: the plane opens an Order of a series, a series shows as a plane of its Orders linked by the edges they declare, and the positions of a picture live with the series']
  [ctx'the Regent, 2026-11-21, V4: b, per EMS; when the ORD is NEM, then it is in the ORD; the EMS config file handles position; the ORD front-matter handles position']
  [ins'open, edit and emit an Order from the plane inside the EMS surface of the Explorer, by the title of the Order']
  [ins'draw a series as a plane of its Orders: each Order a node, and each declared edge between Orders a connector, ref of nem and ref of EMS, as the coherence between Orders declares them']
  [ins'keep the positions of a plane where the signed model says: those of an Order of a series in the EMS.json of its series, those of a loose Order of NEM in its own front-matter, and the computed layout wherever none is stored']
  [conf'the shape of the positions field of EMS.json and of the front-matter of a loose Order, and whether that front-matter enters what --bundle emits, measured before either is written'[hmn]]
  [onlyif'the EMS.json, the coherence between Orders and the EMS surface of EMS-002 are built: steps 2, 3 and 11 of the trail']
  [cnst'the PIN icons wait for the vocabulary of the PIN, step 6 of the trail: until then the two files stay in the table as icons no command names']
  [cnst'a path that does not resolve warns on the plane and never blocks the emission']
  [val'the surface','an Order of a series is opened, edited by its links and emitted from the installed Explorer, and the bundle it writes is the bundle the command line writes for the same source']
  [val'the series','the plane of a series shows every Order and every declared edge of its register, counted against the register']
  [val'the positions','a node moved on the plane is written to the EMS.json of its series, or to the front-matter of a loose Order, and the plane read again shows the same picture; with none stored, the computed layout answers']
];
